  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Alpha. Fixed: == on Server, Session, Window, Pane and Client compares identity rather than reference. Equality for these has always been the server generation plus the typed ID and Equals implemented it, but no operator existed, so two handles read for the same tmux object answered true from Equals and false from ==. All five now carry ==, != and IEquatable<T>. SessionId, WindowId and PaneId no longer throw when sorted: they are record structs, which carry equality and no ordering, so OrderBy and Array.Sort failed at run time with InvalidOperationException. All three implement IComparable<T> and the four relational operators. Breaking: TmuxOutputEvent.PaneId is a PaneId rather than a string, so matching pane output to a handle no longer means parsing the text back; an %output line whose first word is not a pane identifier arrives as a TmuxNotificationEvent, named but unparsed, because a throwing parse in the pump would fault the whole event stream. Changed: PaneActivityHub keys pane wakeups by PaneId, which removes an allocation per chunk a pane writes, and CaptureSignal answers null for text that is not a pane identifier. Added: Session.GetWindowAsync takes a WindowId, matching window_id alone where the string overload also matches window_name. The public API is not settled and may change without notice between prereleases; pin an exact version. Full history: https://github.com/libtmux/libtmux-dotnet/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md",
